  "transcript": [
    {
      "start": 1.81,
      "end": 6.1,
      "text": "You think you see me in the glass?",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6.1,
      "end": 8.1,
      "text": "You think you hear me?",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 8.1,
      "end": 10.1,
      "text": "You better listen fast.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 10.1,
      "end": 12.1,
      "text": "I think I see you.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 12.1,
      "end": 14.1,
      "text": "I've got to see you.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 14.1,
      "end": 16.1,
      "text": "And the only reason",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 16.1,
      "end": 18.1,
      "text": "is you don't believe.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 18.1,
      "end": 22.1,
      "text": "That I'm dead on your own.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 22.1,
      "end": 27.82,
      "text": "Your face turns to stone.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 27.82,
      "end": 30.82,
      "text": "Whatever happened to your life?",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 30.82,
      "end": 34.46,
      "text": "So again, forever",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 34.46,
      "end": 47.32,
      "text": "Never had you as a",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 47.32,
      "end": 49.48,
      "text": "A top-tier dude",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 49.48,
      "end": 51.52,
      "text": "With a sweet love list",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 51.52,
      "end": 53.88,
      "text": "And a silver spoon",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 53.88,
      "end": 56.12,
      "text": "You never had it",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 56.12,
      "end": 58.26,
      "text": "Quite so good",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 58.26,
      "end": 60.44,
      "text": "Because you didn't know",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 60.44,
      "end": 62.68,
      "text": "That you were good",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 62.68,
      "end": 65.53,
      "text": "Time has come to own",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 65.53,
      "end": 70.02,
      "text": "Your turn stands to go",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 70.02,
      "end": 74.34,
      "text": "Whatever happened to your life",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 74.34,
      "end": 78.77,
      "text": "Star wounded lover",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 78.77,
      "end": 437.32,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 148.53,
      "end": 155.13,
      "text": "Some of us might be saying, I've heard that song before.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 437.32,
      "end": 437.96,
      "text": "You probably have.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 438.06,
      "end": 439.3,
      "text": "It was written by John Fogarty",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 439.3,
      "end": 442.34,
      "text": "and recorded by Creedence Clearwater Revival",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 442.34,
      "end": 443.2,
      "text": "many years ago.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 444.48,
      "end": 445.52,
      "text": "Back in the 60s, really.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 446.4,
      "end": 448.94,
      "text": "It was there, though done by T.T. Quick,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 449.08,
      "end": 450.38,
      "text": "who come from New Jersey, I think,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 450.48,
      "end": 452.14,
      "text": "from an album of theirs, which is out",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 452.14,
      "end": 454.66,
      "text": "only on import on Megaforce Records,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 454.76,
      "end": 456.36,
      "text": "incorporated in our country.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 457.8,
      "end": 459.22,
      "text": "T.T. Quick, Fortunate Son,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 459.22,
      "end": 462.92,
      "text": "Before that, Motorhead from the EP The Golden Years and Stone Dead Forever.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 464.42,
      "end": 469.2,
      "text": "That was for a gentleman by the name of James from a lady called Nicky of Hampton Hill.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 469.84,
      "end": 472.64,
      "text": "He wanted to say thanks for taking me to see them.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 472.78,
      "end": 473.72,
      "text": "I thoroughly enjoyed them.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 473.9,
      "end": 477.46,
      "text": "Also, hello to Steve and hope we see him soon.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 479.39,
      "end": 483.65,
      "text": "Friday the 1st of June, I should say hello to a wonderful fellow by the name of Trevor.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 484.33,
      "end": 486.65,
      "text": "Janet has sent me this card from Bangor and County Down.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 487.41,
      "end": 489.19,
      "text": "On the 3rd of this month, couple of days time,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 489.25,
      "end": 491.57,
      "text": "it will be the first anniversary of them getting together.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 492.17,
      "end": 493.69,
      "text": "If I tell you Trevor on behalf of Janet,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 494.57,
      "end": 496.35,
      "text": "that he really, or she really,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 496.77,
      "end": 498.69,
      "text": "thanks you for the love and the laughs,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 499.23,
      "end": 501.49,
      "text": "and also just says a happy new year, and a happy year.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 502.86,
      "end": 504.8,
      "text": "Okay, how are you over there in Ireland tonight?",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 505.5,
      "end": 507.56,
      "text": "Phil Samuels, Stafford Road,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 507.7,
      "end": 509.8,
      "text": "the Ford House's Wolverhampton, I've heard that name before.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 511.06,
      "end": 513.16,
      "text": "Wanted me to say hello to Colin and Keith,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 513.16,
      "end": 514.92,
      "text": "the two Dyson brothers, Mark and Paul,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 515.04,
      "end": 517.24,
      "text": "Leroy Sticky, I think it is, Baker,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 518.2,
      "end": 520.24,
      "text": "A. Davis and a special hello to Pauline,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 520.44,
      "end": 523.0,
      "text": "the lady who runs the John Sykes Appreciation Society.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 523.0,
      "end": 523.22,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 523.58,
      "end": 526.84,
      "text": "Hope that she's listening, and hello to Philip Lynott as well.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 528.22,
      "end": 533.02,
      "text": "...was Jaguar from our repeat session by then.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 533.02,
      "end": 1165.25,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 1165.25,
      "end": 1166.99,
      "text": "The track was called Long Shadows.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1167.17,
      "end": 1170.71,
      "text": "Before that, you heard something by Utopia from their new album, Oblivion.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1171.05,
      "end": 1172.33,
      "text": "The track was Cry, baby.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1178.06,
      "end": 1181.08,
      "text": "24 minutes past ten, the Friday Rock Show from BBC Radio 1.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1181.44,
      "end": 1190.37,
      "text": "Ian Rhodes lives in Rose or Rosie, Shiplex,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1190.37,
      "end": 1192.09,
      "text": "which is near Bradford somewhere.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1192.35,
      "end": 1193.45,
      "text": "Not seen that address before.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1193.59,
      "end": 1194.17,
      "text": "How are you, Ian?",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1194.79,
      "end": 1196.31,
      "text": "Dear Thomas, would you please say hello?",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1196.47,
      "end": 1198.39,
      "text": "To all me mates, give them all a mention.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1198.63,
      "end": 1203.55,
      "text": "E.G. Stuart Lidbury, Nicholas, Dave, Wayne, Chris, Brett, John",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1203.55,
      "end": 1205.41,
      "text": "and everybody in the Crescent in Bradford.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1206.46,
      "end": 1207.36,
      "text": "From Ian Rhodes who says,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1207.44,
      "end": 1209.92,
      "text": "P.S. Black Sabbath should have sued Ian Gillan.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1214.59,
      "end": 1216.69,
      "text": "Hello to a gentleman who's 13 years of age.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1216.73,
      "end": 1217.95,
      "text": "His name is Mark Brown.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1218.19,
      "end": 1221.29,
      "text": "He lives at Despenser Gardens, Riverside in Cardiff.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1223.08,
      "end": 1224.92,
      "text": "Mark Brown, I know you listen to this program.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1225.3,
      "end": 1233.35,
      "text": "best wishes from me best wishes from your dad whom i met the other day nice man this is killer",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1233.35,
      "end": 1244.75,
      "text": "saxon from the album wheels of steel 747 strangers in the night and before that you heard a belgian",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1885.08,
      "end": 1890.16,
      "text": "band who are out on mausoleum records a record label that's actually from this country based in",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1890.16,
      "end": 1896.14,
      "text": "robberham belgian band by the name of killer their three-piece band called shorty spooky and double",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1896.14,
      "end": 1900.04,
      "text": "bear. Double bear.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1900.82,
      "end": 1902.28,
      "text": "The album title is Shockwaves.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1902.38,
      "end": 1904.02,
      "text": "The track was called In the Eye of My Gun.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1907.0,
      "end": 1908.26,
      "text": "And the saxophone track was for",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1908.26,
      "end": 1910.28,
      "text": "some mates of Tim Lowe, who sent me",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1910.28,
      "end": 1912.42,
      "text": "a very nice postcard, at Pannafort Point",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1912.42,
      "end": 1913.86,
      "text": "in Loo Island in Cornwall.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1915.12,
      "end": 1916.44,
      "text": "Hello to the Fifth Form Rockers,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1916.56,
      "end": 1918.96,
      "text": "all doing exams and stuff like that. Lots of luck.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1919.73,
      "end": 1920.89,
      "text": "Particular hello to Mouthy",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1920.89,
      "end": 1922.23,
      "text": "and Nigel and Chris and Naughty.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1922.43,
      "end": 1924.49,
      "text": "Andrew Peachy, how peachly possibly.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1925.46,
      "end": 1927.02,
      "text": "Hello to Mum. That's the mum",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1927.02,
      "end": 1929.06,
      "text": "of Tim Lowe. It's her birthday.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1929.06,
      "end": 1929.76,
      "text": "or was recently.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1933.41,
      "end": 1935.53,
      "text": "Martin, the maniac from Bristol,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1935.81,
      "end": 1937.13,
      "text": "wants to wish a very happy birthday",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1937.13,
      "end": 1938.45,
      "text": "to his girlfriend, Abby,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1938.69,
      "end": 1941.29,
      "text": "in Westcombe, or Westcombe, I guess,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1941.37,
      "end": 1942.71,
      "text": "in Wilshire, on June the 1st.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1943.27,
      "end": 1944.57,
      "text": "Must learn to read one of these days.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1944.99,
      "end": 1947.21,
      "text": "I need a holiday, and I'm getting one soon.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1949.18,
      "end": 1950.4,
      "text": "Abby, happy birthday",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1950.4,
      "end": 1951.86,
      "text": "from Martin, the maniac.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1954.65,
      "end": 1956.39,
      "text": "Nice car here from Sue Madison of Manchester.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1958.1,
      "end": 1958.82,
      "text": "Hello to her boyfriend",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1958.82,
      "end": 1959.78,
      "text": "by the name of Wayne.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1960.14,
      "end": 1961.68,
      "text": "19 today. Happy birthday, Wayne.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1961.98,
      "end": 1963.78,
      "text": "It seems a mention would really cheer him up",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1963.78,
      "end": 1965.06,
      "text": "as he always listens to the program.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1965.42,
      "end": 1969.44,
      "text": "At the moment, though, he's studying for his first-year degree exams at Preston Poly.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1969.98,
      "end": 1974.02,
      "text": "Would you please tell him that I love him very much, and I will see him soon after his exams.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1974.6,
      "end": 1977.54,
      "text": "Tell him very much. Love, Sue Madison, Manchester.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1977.98,
      "end": 1979.32,
      "text": "Wayne, she's thinking of you.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1979.82,
      "end": 1980.8,
      "text": "But keep studying.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1984.58,
      "end": 1985.56,
      "text": "Here's Little Steven.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1986.06,
      "end": 1993.26,
      "text": "That was Chasar, from a cassette album that they're selling at gigs.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1993.26,
      "end": 2606.06,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 2611.06,
      "end": 2612.7,
      "text": "The track was called Visions of Time.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2614.09,
      "end": 2617.37,
      "text": "Before that, Little Steven, who's coming over to do a gig shortly in this country.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2617.37,
      "end": 2623.58,
      "text": "his new single is called out of the darkness 11 and a half minutes to 11 the friday rock show",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2623.58,
      "end": 2634.29,
      "text": "rock show bbc radio one record request and dedication to ann marie mo was wanley stu kirk",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2634.29,
      "end": 2642.35,
      "text": "and stevie john and anybody else who knows me me being bill the holy one putin also what's a",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2642.35,
      "end": 2647.49,
      "text": "special hello to jan and sarah who've got their own levels in two weeks lots of luck",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2652.02,
      "end": 2653.74,
      "text": "Barry Lund is in Grimsby.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2654.2,
      "end": 2659.7,
      "text": "And he says, dear Thomas, please play a request for Mr. Sean Parkinson at the moment in Stafford.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2660.26,
      "end": 2664.78,
      "text": "Anything by Queen or anything of your choice would go down very, very well with Sean.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2664.88,
      "end": 2666.22,
      "text": "Would you mention his name more than once?",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2666.34,
      "end": 2669.62,
      "text": "Sean Parkinson, Sean Parkinson, Sean Parkinson, Stafford.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2671.36,
      "end": 2671.98,
      "text": "How are you, Doc?",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2672.1,
      "end": 2672.78,
      "text": "Hope you're all right.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2675.14,
      "end": 2680.01,
      "text": "Very best wishes from Barry Lund of Willow's Estate, Grimsby.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2680.49,
      "end": 2685.21,
      "text": "A couple of fellas signed this letter.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2685.37,
      "end": 2687.05,
      "text": "Lance Owen and Andrew Robinson.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2687.41,
      "end": 2695.41,
      "text": "want me to say hello to ian morgan happy birthday today and i mentioned to you ian morgan from",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2695.41,
      "end": 2705.01,
      "text": "everybody in strewed and everybody at archway school in that said town that's jaguar from our",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2705.01,
      "end": 3220.2,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 3220.2,
      "end": 3224.22,
      "text": "repeat session by then the track you heard was called last flight and before that you heard a",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3224.22,
      "end": 3229.42,
      "text": "band called young blood from an ep four tracks on it 12 inch it is called first blood the track was",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3229.42,
      "end": 3233.66,
      "text": "called hold on to love it's just coming up to a minute to 11 so i better squeeze this in because",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3233.66,
      "end": 3236.64,
      "text": "has been requested between 8 o'clock and 11 o'clock",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3236.64,
      "end": 3237.88,
      "text": "to be read out on the radio.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3238.1,
      "end": 3239.4,
      "text": "It's from a lady called Fiona,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3240.08,
      "end": 3243.08,
      "text": "who lives in East Kilbride in Newlandsmuir,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3243.16,
      "end": 3244.18,
      "text": "I think it's possibly said.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3244.56,
      "end": 3246.34,
      "text": "Dear Thomas fans, please read out this message",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3246.34,
      "end": 3248.52,
      "text": "for my boyfriend, Gary Stewart,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3249.0,
      "end": 3250.62,
      "text": "for his 18th on the 2nd of June.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3250.72,
      "end": 3252.04,
      "text": "Tell him that I love him very much,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3252.38,
      "end": 3253.76,
      "text": "that I hope he has a great birthday.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3254.34,
      "end": 3257.92,
      "text": "Well, Fiona, of the indecipherable second name",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3257.92,
      "end": 3260.64,
      "text": "of Windermere, Newlandsmuir, East Kilbride,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3260.64,
      "end": 3262.54,
      "text": "I hope you're going to be there to make it a good birthday for him.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3262.54,
      "end": 3283.42,
      "text": "And I've just found a card from another lady called Fiona. This is Fiona Dugdale, of Ambleside in Cumbria. Watch out, how are you? Please say hi to everybody who was at Donington last year, especially Kevin, Chris, Stuart, Fiona, A, Bucket Albert T, sounds like a name of a car, Bucket Albert T, Dennis and HJ, plus anybody else who's going to go this year, and I'll see you there. You indeed will.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3283.42,
      "end": 3290.2,
      "text": "And, of course, later, at about 20 minutes past 11, you will hear the set that was laid down by ZZ Top, tonight on this year's programme.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3290.8,
      "end": 3294.62,
      "text": "And then Fiona says, or would you please send me a signed photograph of yourself?",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3295.14,
      "end": 3297.34,
      "text": "Well, unfortunately, I can't stand looking at them.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3297.52,
      "end": 3301.94,
      "text": "But I saw a photograph of myself in the Daily Mirror the other day, which was really quite astonishing.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3302.46,
      "end": 3304.82,
      "text": "Because it was taken back in about 1971.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3305.42,
      "end": 3306.66,
      "text": "Looked like a blooming walrus.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3306.66,
      "end": 3415.0,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 3420.0,
      "end": 3520.09,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 3520.97,
      "end": 3521.73,
      "text": "Spajococca.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3522.43,
      "end": 3525.09,
      "text": "That's his new single. It is called Civilised Man.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3525.09,
      "end": 3534.52,
      "text": "4 minutes past 11, time for the Friday Night Connection here on the Friday Rock Show from BBC Radio 1",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3534.52,
      "end": 3536.22,
      "text": "Last week we played you these tracks",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3536.22,
      "end": 3540.48,
      "text": "Down below the borderline from the last record album by Little Feet",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3540.48,
      "end": 3544.94,
      "text": "Those Shoes from the long run by the Eagles",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3544.94,
      "end": 3549.22,
      "text": "And One Step Ahead of the Blues from Grasshopper by J.J. Cale",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3549.22,
      "end": 3553.51,
      "text": "Hardly anybody got it right",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3553.51,
      "end": 3556.78,
      "text": "Must have been a complex one",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3556.78,
      "end": 3559.84,
      "text": "Quite simple really, Little Feet",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3559.84,
      "end": 3561.52,
      "text": "those shoes",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3561.52,
      "end": 3564.04,
      "text": "one step ahead of the Blues.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3565.81,
      "end": 3566.51,
      "text": "One winner,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3566.91,
      "end": 3568.93,
      "text": "and who cops the £12 record token",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3568.93,
      "end": 3570.91,
      "text": "this week? The gentleman who lives just around",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3570.91,
      "end": 3571.97,
      "text": "the corner from me, virtually.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3573.52,
      "end": 3575.7,
      "text": "By standing on top of this building, I can see his pad.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3576.24,
      "end": 3577.52,
      "text": "Sussex Gardens, London",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3577.52,
      "end": 3579.38,
      "text": "W2, the home of Paul Joyce.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3579.74,
      "end": 3581.3,
      "text": "Congratulations, £12 record token,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3581.36,
      "end": 3583.04,
      "text": "and a few other goodies coming your way, sir.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3592.65,
      "end": 3594.13,
      "text": "Now, Paul Joyce wants me to",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3594.13,
      "end": 3596.15,
      "text": "say hello to Paul and Andrew Hopkins.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3596.15,
      "end": 3598.7,
      "text": "Now we've got that over, we shall",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3598.7,
      "end": 3600.74,
      "text": "now go into the Friday Night",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3600.74,
      "end": 3601.86,
      "text": "Connection of Paul.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3602.64,
      "end": 3604.62,
      "text": "Three bits of music, the connection's in there",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3604.62,
      "end": 3606.42,
      "text": "somewhere. It's down to you",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3606.42,
      "end": 3611.22,
      "text": "to get it out. My Connection, put together",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3611.22,
      "end": 4457.62,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 4457.62,
      "end": 4459.36,
      "text": "by Paul Joyce of Sussex Gardens,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4459.54,
      "end": 4461.64,
      "text": "London, W2. If you think you know the answer",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4461.64,
      "end": 4463.6,
      "text": "and it certainly is in there somewhere, and it's",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4463.6,
      "end": 4465.64,
      "text": "not that hard, jot it on a",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4465.64,
      "end": 4467.6,
      "text": "postcard, back of an envelope, whatever you care to",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4467.6,
      "end": 4469.56,
      "text": "employ, as long as it's written, send it to",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4469.56,
      "end": 4471.4,
      "text": "the Friday Night Connection,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4471.74,
      "end": 4473.54,
      "text": "the Friday Rock Show, BBC",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4473.54,
      "end": 4475.3,
      "text": "Radio 1, London,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4475.3,
      "end": 4477.36,
      "text": "W1A4WW",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4477.36,
      "end": 4479.7,
      "text": "The address once again is",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4479.7,
      "end": 4480.74,
      "text": "The Friday Night Connection",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4480.74,
      "end": 4482.06,
      "text": "The Friday Rock Show",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4482.06,
      "end": 4483.72,
      "text": "BBC Radio 1",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4483.72,
      "end": 4486.78,
      "text": "London W1A4WW",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4486.78,
      "end": 4489.72,
      "text": "Please do not forget to put together",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4489.72,
      "end": 4491.06,
      "text": "A connection of your own",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4491.06,
      "end": 4493.64,
      "text": "And a bon chance",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4493.64,
      "end": 4498.2,
      "text": "20 minutes past 11",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4498.2,
      "end": 4499.7,
      "text": "Outcoming on the Friday Rock Show",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4499.7,
      "end": 4501.28,
      "text": "At about 29 minutes past",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4501.28,
      "end": 4502.9,
      "text": "We have ZZ Top from Donington",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4502.9,
      "end": 4504.26,
      "text": "As they were last year",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4504.26,
      "end": 4506.22,
      "text": "But we've got Jaguar here",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4506.22,
      "end": 4508.76,
      "text": "Two good, excellent tracks by them",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4508.76,
      "end": 4510.92,
      "text": "Back to back. This one is Stand Up.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4511.5,
      "end": 4516.9,
      "text": "That's there by Jaguar from our session by then.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4973.08,
      "end": 4975.72,
      "text": "That was called This Time. Before that you heard Stand Up.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4976.02,
      "end": 4978.74,
      "text": "And since they've recorded that session, they've actually got a new drummer,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4978.86,
      "end": 4981.02,
      "text": "a fellow by the name of Gary Davis. Good name for a disc jockey.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4981.16,
      "end": 4984.38,
      "text": "They've got an LP coming out late in June, which is called This Time,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4984.48,
      "end": 4986.7,
      "text": "and which will include the tracks that you heard on the session tonight.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4987.06,
      "end": 4991.8,
      "text": "And they've also got a gig on June the 20th at the Bristol Bridge Inn in Bristol.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4992.08,
      "end": 4993.42,
      "text": "Good luck to Jaguar.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4993.42,
      "end": 5002.26,
      "text": "The Friday Rock Show from BBC Radio 1.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5002.32,
      "end": 5005.28,
      "text": "Now we're going to rebroadcast the set that was put down on the stage",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5005.28,
      "end": 5009.36,
      "text": "at Donington 1983 by the band from Texas called ZZ Top.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5009.74,
      "end": 5011.28,
      "text": "Just a little word of advice, though.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5011.36,
      "end": 5013.84,
      "text": "This was recorded by the BBC, produced by Tony Wilson,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5013.96,
      "end": 5015.72,
      "text": "but mixed in the United States of America.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5016.18,
      "end": 5019.44,
      "text": "And I think it's quite a flat mix, so a suggestion to you.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5019.52,
      "end": 5022.34,
      "text": "Maybe you could turn up the presence control on your stereo.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5022.34,
      "end": 5026.36,
      "text": "But nonetheless, whatever I think of it, it's absolutely excellent.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5026.74,
      "end": 5029.68,
      "text": "Donington 83, the band ZZ Top.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5030.18,
      "end": 5035.58,
      "text": "ZZ Top, as they were at Donington last year.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6784.65,
      "end": 6787.13,
      "text": "Billy Gibbons, Dusty Hill, and Frank Beard.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6790.14,
      "end": 6794.4,
      "text": "This year at Donington, ACDC, Van Halen, Gary Moore, except Y&T and Motley Crue.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6795.1,
      "end": 6799.0,
      "text": "Production by Tony Wilson, who's getting married tomorrow, and I'm his best man.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6799.16,
      "end": 6804.24,
      "text": "Don't worry, Maggie, I'll get him to the church on time, but I cannot guarantee his condition.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6805.33,
      "end": 6809.38,
      "text": "I'm off for a month. Shouts of, whee! All around, I'm sure.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6809.38,
      "end": 6811.54,
      "text": "Andy Batten-Foster will be with you with the good music",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6811.54,
      "end": 6813.94,
      "text": "I'm actually going to Antarctica for two weeks",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6813.94,
      "end": 6815.26,
      "text": "And then to Ibiza for two weeks",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6815.26,
      "end": 6816.54,
      "text": "Talk about a contrast",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6816.54,
      "end": 6820.28,
      "text": "News is next on MediaWave on VHF Radio 2",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6820.28,
      "end": 6822.04,
      "text": "I'm Tommy Vance on behalf of everybody",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6822.04,
      "end": 6824.08,
      "text": "On the music side of Radio 1, you take care",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6824.08,
      "end": 6825.74,
      "text": "You're well thought of around here",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6825.74,
      "end": 6826.86,
      "text": "God bless you, goodnight",
      "source": "uncertain"
    }
  ]
}